2}}$ if there exist ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ such that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2} & =b \\\\ {x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ -3 \\\\ k\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}5{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=-3 \\\\ {x}_{1}-{x}_{2}=-3 \\\\ 2{x}_{1}-{x}_{2}=k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo solve the system above, we set up and row reduce an augmented matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & [\\begin{aligned}5 & 1 & -3 \\\\ 1 & -1 & -3 \\\\ 2 & -1 & k\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & ↔{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & -3 \\\\ 5 & 1 & -3 \\\\ 2 & -1 & k\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-5{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 6 & 12 \\\\ 2 & -1 & k\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 6 & 12 \\\\ 0 & 1 & k+6\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :=\\frac{1}{6}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & k+6\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & k+4\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe third row of the augmented matrix now corresponds to the equation $0{x}_{1}+0{x}_{2}=k+4.$ Therefore, the system has a solution only if\n\n$$\n0=k+4\\,⇒\\,k=-4.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186369652 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186369653 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186369652 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186369654 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186369652 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186369655 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186369652 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186369656 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186369652 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186369657 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186369652 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186369652 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186369652 #edb/ref 1078 