:={R}_{3}+(-2){R}_{2}$ involves adding a multiple of one row to another row,  so it does not change the determinant.\n\n- The operation ${R}_{1}:=2{R}_{1}$ involves multiplying a row by $2,$ so the determinant is multiplied by $2$ as well.\n\nTherefore, we only have to multiply the determinant by $2.$ Consequently, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(B) & =2det(A) \\\\  & =2\\cdot 8 \\\\  & =16.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186385430 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186385431 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186385430 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186385432 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186385430 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186385433 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186385430 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186385434 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186385430 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186385435 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186385430 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186385430 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186385430 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186385432 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186385430 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "1b2cf6c5-f5c6-5493-95a1-8c32ef657814" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186385431 #edb/ref 1080 "-16" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186385431 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186385431 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "70033240-b70d-5bd1-a4ed-4790885b2931" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186385432 #edb/ref 1080 "16" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186385432 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186385432 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "178a3520-0f80-5c41-83eb-f447ec674bdc" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186385433 #edb/ref 1080 "8" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186385433 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186385433 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "b5f49b63-abb6-55d5-bfcd-031cbf531d3f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186385434 #edb/ref 1080 "-4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186385434 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref